            "value": "ITC's SOTP derives 60% value from cigarettes (₹3,52,000 cr), where the 16x multiple reflects global tobacco peer median 11-13x plus a 30% Indian regulatory & export premium — defensible given FY27 FCF conversion and pricing power. The 31% FMCG contribution (₹1,80,000 cr at 40x EBITDA) is the key swing factor; it assumes HUL-grade peer multiples (50-55x) discounted 20% for execution track record, reasonable for India's #2 consumer player after HUL but requiring margin acceleration to 22%+ to justify. Corporate overhead capitalised at 10x (₹5,000 cr) and a 7% conglomerate discount (reflecting active operational management vs. pure holdco) yield a target of ₹429/share, 7.7% below CMP of ₹465, implying HOLD: upside capped until cigarettes multiple re-rates above 16x (unlikely without global M&A/demerger discourse) or FMCG margins crystallise above 21% (watch FY28 delivery). Key inflection: if FMCG organic revenue sustains 15%+ growth and margins expand to 22%+, multiple could reset to 45-50x, driving +₹50,000 cr EV swing; conversely, cigarette tax pressures or FMCG competitive intensity could justify lower numbers.",
